{
  "about": "Reference vectors for PROTOCOL.md \"Input mapping\". All byte values are hex. \"payload\" is the message payload and \"frame\" the whole inner message ([type][4-byte length][payload]) before SECURE wraps it. An encoder must produce the bytes in \"frames\" from the listed values and a decoder the values from the bytes. \"ignored\" lists messages a host must drop without acting, and \"longer\" messages whose extra bytes it must skip. \"scroll\" and \"relative\" give the deltas a host uses (before any rounding of its own); an entry marked \"ignored\" scrolls nothing. \"keyFlags\" gives the flag bits a host actually uses. \"text\" gives what a host types for an INPUT_TEXT payload: the steps in order, where a \"key\" step is a press and release of that key (codes in \"textKeys\") and adjacent typed pieces count as one \"text\" step (a host may type them in smaller pieces, never splitting a code point).",
